  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "caption": "Summary",
      "html": "<p>This optional unit adds 50 words that occur 12 times in the New Testament and are not in Machen&#x27;s lessons: 28 nouns, 15 verbs and 7 other words. Nothing in the course waits for them; they are here so that you can read the New Testament with the lexicon open less often. Learn them on the Words track: recognize, recall, type, type with accents.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "caption": "Built from words you know",
      "html": "<p>These verbs are a preposition plus a verb from the lessons; the meaning usually follows from the parts: ἀναπίπτω (πίπτω); ἐξάγω (ἄγω); μεταβαίνω (βαίνω).</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "caption": "Common confusion",
      "html": "<p>Look-alikes that differ by one letter: αὐλή (court-yard) and φυλή (a tribe); βῆμα (a judgment seat) and ῥῆμα (a word); δέομαι (I request) and δέχομαι (I receive); ἔθος (a custom) and ἔθνος (a nation); ἔσωθεν (from within) and ἔξωθεν (from without); λιμός (a famine) and λίθος (a stone); μωρός (stupid) and μέρος (a part); ὀδούς (a tooth) and ὁδός (a road). Feminine although they end in -ος, like ὁδός: λιμός, ῥάβδος. Neuter nouns in -ος with the genitive -ους, like γένος: ἔθος, κράτος.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "caption": "Source",
      "html": "<p>Words chosen by their New Testament frequency (MorphGNT); glosses after Jeffrey Dodson&#x27;s Greek-English lexicon (public domain).</p>"
    },
